# Windows/React Native native-build requirement — do not remove without reading this.
#
# pnpm's default isolated store puts every package under a long, hashed directory:
#   node_modules/.pnpm/react-native-safe-area-cont_03cece60fd19a98b0ba6b6504f440e7d/node_modules/<pkg>/
# CMake mirrors each source file's absolute path underneath the native build directory, so that ~85-char
# store segment is duplicated into every object-file path. ninja.exe is not long-path aware (the
# LongPathsEnabled registry setting does not help it) and hard-fails at Windows' 260-char limit with:
#   ninja: error: Stat(...RNCSafeAreaViewShadowNode.cpp.o): Filename longer than 260 characters
#
# A hoisted layout resolves packages at node_modules/<pkg>/ instead, removing that segment and roughly
# 85 characters from every mirrored path — the difference between ~263 (fails) and ~243 (builds).
# Shortening the CMake staging root (see apps/mobile/android/build.gradle) was necessary but not
# sufficient on its own; both changes together are what make the Android native build work on Windows.
#
# Trade-off accepted deliberately: hoisting is less strict than pnpm's isolated default, so a package
# can import a dependency it does not declare. That is a real downside, but it is the standard
# React Native + pnpm + Windows configuration, and the alternative is no Android build on this machine.
node-linker=hoisted
